    "schema": "{ cwe: {CWE-id -> target}, class: {redstrike-class-slug -> target} }  where target = {path,id} | {candidates:[{path,id}, ...]}",
    "purpose": "Deterministic CWE/finding-class -> VRT crosswalk. So a bug-bounty finding's VRT is RESOLVED from the pinned taxonomy, not improvised (the fabricated-VRT incident). scripts/vrt.py reads this; resolve_finding_vrt() looks a finding's category.cwe / executor class up here and returns the real VRT path + the taxonomy's own baseline priority.",
    "authoritative_source": "The PINNED taxonomy skills/bug-bounty/refs/vrt/vulnerability-rating-taxonomy.json is the single source of truth for priorities. This file carries NO priorities of its own on purpose (anti-drift): every `priority`/`baseline` is read back from the taxonomy node at resolve time. EVERY `path` here MUST resolve to a real taxonomy node — scripts/validate.py HARD-FAILS if any crosswalk target does not exist.",
    "built_against_taxonomy": {
      "upstream_source": "bugcrowd/vulnerability-rating-taxonomy",
      "upstream_ref": "20cc155a74c7f9136fed714acc298f281bd793d3",
      "upstream_version": "2026-07-08T00:00:00+00:00"
    },
    "paths_are_id_paths": "Each `path` is the node ids joined by ' > ' (stable identifiers), e.g. 'server_side_injection > sql_injection'. scripts/vrt.py path_exists() also accepts the equivalent display-name path and a bare leaf id.",
    "defaults_not_verdicts": "A crosswalk hit is a DEFAULT SEED, not a final rating. The returned priority is the taxonomy baseline; a submission may deviate ONLY via finding.vrt.priority_basis='argued-elevation'/'argued-reduction' with a non-empty priority_rationale (anti-inflation, enforced by elevation_errors()). Where a class has no single VRT home, a `candidates` list is given and resolve_finding_vrt() returns the first that resolves (the primary); operators pick among the alternatives.",
    "coverage": "A CWE/class absent here is a LEGITIMATE state (resolve returns None) — business-logic, race-condition-only, memory-safety and other classes with no distinct VRT node are intentionally left for the operator/generator to place. Unmapped != invalid."
  },

